</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Why Arjun uses ThreadIt:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>He has money but not time</li>
<li>He knows what he wants (a formal shirt, a pair of chinos) but doesn&#39;t want to spend 2 hours getting it</li>
<li>He already trusts local stores — he&#39;s bought from them before</li>
<li>30-minute delivery fits his lifestyle</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>What could stop Arjun:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>If the catalog looks cheap or poorly photographed — he&#39;ll compare it unfavorably to Myntra&#39;s polished UI</li>
<li>If the first delivery is late or the product doesn&#39;t match the listing — he won&#39;t give a second chance</li>
<li>If the delivery fee feels too high relative to what he&#39;s ordering (₹50 delivery on a ₹500 item feels steep; ₹50 on a ₹2,000 item is fine)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Arjun&#39;s activation trigger:</strong> &quot;I need something by tomorrow and I don&#39;t want to go to the market.&quot;</p>
