<p><strong>Why Priya uses ThreadIt:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>She wants trendy clothes NOW, not in 5 days</li>
<li>She&#39;s already buying from local stores but hates the commute from campus/hostel</li>
<li>She&#39;s price-sensitive but values convenience — will pay ₹30–₹50 for delivery if it saves her a trip</li>
<li>Social proof matters — if her friends use it, she will too</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>What could stop Priya:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>If prices on ThreadIt are higher than what she&#39;d pay in-store (she will compare)</li>
<li>If there&#39;s no way to see &quot;what&#39;s trending&quot; or &quot;new arrivals&quot; — she browses before buying</li>
<li>If the app feels like it&#39;s for &quot;aunties&quot; — design and brand positioning must feel young</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Priya&#39;s activation trigger:</strong> &quot;I saw this cute top at a store last week, I wonder if I can just order it.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[!NOTE]<br><strong>Priya is our most powerful growth channel, not our most profitable customer.</strong> Her AOV is low, but she&#39;s the one who will share the app in WhatsApp groups, post about it on Instagram stories, and drive viral adoption. Acquire Priya for growth, monetize Arjun for revenue.</p>
</blockquote>
