<li>She trusts specific stores — &quot;Rajesh bhai at XYZ store always picks the right size for my son&quot;</li>
<li>Higher AOV because she buys for the whole family</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>What could stop Meera:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>If she can&#39;t specify the store she wants to order from — she has store loyalty</li>
<li>If the return process is complicated — she&#39;s buying for kids, sizes will be wrong sometimes</li>
<li>If there&#39;s no way to message the store owner (&quot;Do you have this in blue? What size do you suggest for a 4-year-old?&quot;)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Meera&#39;s activation trigger:</strong> &quot;My son needs new school uniform trousers and I don&#39;t have time to go to the shop today.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[!IMPORTANT]<br><strong>The chat-with-store feature is not a &quot;nice to have&quot; for Meera — it&#39;s a dealbreaker.</strong> She needs to communicate with the vendor the way she would in person. This must be in the MVP.</p>
</blockquote>
