<p><strong>Key UX nudge:</strong> The exchange option is shown FIRST and marked &quot;Recommended.&quot; It&#39;s free. The return option is shown second with a ₹49 fee visible. This design deliberately pushes toward exchanges, which is better for all parties (Chapter 10).</p>
<hr>
<h1>Chapter 14 — Vendor App</h1>
<h2>Design Philosophy: &quot;Uncle-Proof Design&quot;</h2>
<p>The vendor app has a fundamentally different design constraint than the customer app. Our vendors are:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Store owners aged 35–55</strong> who are not digital natives</li>
<li>Using <strong>mid-range Android phones</strong> with possibly small screens</li>
<li><strong>Multitasking</strong> between in-store customers and the app</li>
<li><strong>Not going to read instructions</strong> — the app must be self-explanatory</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>[!IMPORTANT]<br><strong>The &quot;Uncle Test&quot;:</strong> If a 50-year-old store owner in Fancy Bazaar who uses only WhatsApp and YouTube cannot figure out how to accept an order within 10 seconds of hearing the notification, we have failed. Every screen must pass this test.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Design rules:</strong></p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Rule</th>
<th>Implementation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>Large tap targets</strong></td>
<td>Minimum 48dp touch targets. Buttons are full-width where possible.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Minimal text</strong></td>
<td>Icons + short labels. No paragraphs. No tooltips.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>High contrast</strong></td>
<td>Dark text on light background. Red for reject, green for accept. No subtle colors.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>No nested menus</strong></td>
<td>No hamburger menus. Bottom tab navigation only. Maximum 4 tabs.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Font size</strong></td>
<td>Minimum 16sp for body text, 20sp+ for key information (order total, item count)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Language</strong></td>
<td>Hindi + English mixed (Hinglish) by default. Assamese language support in v1.1.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Sound</strong></td>
<td>Order notifications use a loud, distinct sound. Not a gentle chime — a sound that cuts through store noise.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Screen Inventory</h2>
<pre><code>VENDOR APP — SCREEN MAP

┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                  │
│  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────────┐   │
│  │DASHBOARD │  │ ORDERS   │  │   CATALOG    │   │
│  │  (Home)  │  │          │  │              │   │
