└──────────────────────────────────┘
</code></pre>
<h3>Design Principles for Rider App</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Principle</th>
<th>Implementation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>One-handed operation</strong></td>
<td>Rider may be holding the phone while standing with the bike. All buttons are at bottom of screen, within thumb reach.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>No typing required</strong></td>
<td>Everything is tap-based. OTP is entered by the CUSTOMER (shown on their app), rider just taps &quot;Delivered.&quot; No text input needed.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Minimal data usage</strong></td>
<td>Maps load via Google Maps intent (opens Google Maps app) rather than embedded maps. Reduces data cost for riders.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Loud notifications</strong></td>
<td>Same as vendor app — order requests use a distinct, loud sound.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Offline resilience</strong></td>
<td>If rider loses connectivity during delivery, last known state is cached. Reconnect syncs automatically.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Battery efficient</strong></td>
<td>Minimize background location tracking. Only track when rider is on an active delivery.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<h3>Screen 4–6: Earnings, History, Profile</h3>
<p><strong>Earnings:</strong> Daily/weekly summary. Per-delivery breakdown. Next payout date.</p>
<p><strong>History:</strong> List of past deliveries with date, route, payout.</p>
<p><strong>Profile:</strong> Name, phone, vehicle details, bank account for payouts.</p>
<hr>
<h1>Chapter 16 — Admin Dashboard</h1>
<h2>Design Philosophy</h2>
<p>The admin dashboard is the <strong>operations command center.</strong> It&#39;s used by the founding team (initially the founder and CTO) to monitor everything, intervene in problems, and track business health.</p>
<p><strong>It must be:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Real-time</strong> — 30-second refresh on live data. Critical alerts trigger browser notifications.</li>
<li><strong>Action-oriented</strong> — Every problem shown must have an action button next to it.</li>
<li><strong>Simple</strong> — No complex BI tool. No pivot tables. Clear numbers, clear status, clear actions.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Built as:</strong> Web app (React). Desktop-first. No mobile optimization needed — this is used on a laptop.</p>
