<h1>Chapter 24 — Go-To-Market Strategy</h1>
<h2>GTM Phases</h2>
<h3>Phase 0: Pre-Launch (4 Weeks Before Launch)</h3>
<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Build supply (vendors) and create demand anticipation (customer waitlist).</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Activity</th>
<th>Detail</th>
<th>Budget</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>Vendor onboarding</strong></td>
<td>Field team onboards 15–20 stores in Zone 1. Follow the onboarding playbook (Chapter 11).</td>
<td>₹0 (team salary already counted)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Waitlist landing page</strong></td>
<td>Simple website: &quot;ThreadIt is coming to Guwahati. Get clothes from local stores in 30 minutes. Join the waitlist.&quot; Collects phone numbers.</td>
<td>₹2,000–₹5,000 (domain + hosting)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Social media presence</strong></td>
<td>Create Instagram + Facebook pages. Post teaser content: &quot;Coming soon to Guwahati,&quot; &quot;Which store should we add first?&quot; polls, behind-the-scenes of onboarding.</td>
<td>₹0 (organic content)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>College ambassador recruitment</strong></td>
<td>Recruit 5–10 college ambassadors from GU, Cotton University, Royal Global. Offer: free orders + referral commission (₹20 per new user who orders).</td>
<td>₹0 upfront (pay per conversion)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Local influencer seeding</strong></td>
<td>Identify 3–5 Guwahati-based Instagram influencers (5K–50K followers). Offer free orders in exchange for launch-day coverage.</td>
<td>₹5,000–₹15,000 (product cost)</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<h3>Phase 1: Launch Week (High-Intensity)</h3>
<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Get 100+ app downloads and 20+ orders in the first week.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Activity</th>
<th>Detail</th>
<th>Budget</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>&quot;Free Delivery Week&quot;</strong></td>
<td>All orders get free delivery for the first 7 days. Creates urgency and removes friction for first-time users.</td>
<td>₹5,000–₹10,000 (subsidized delivery)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Waitlist notification</strong></td>
<td>SMS all waitlist signups: &quot;ThreadIt is LIVE! Order now, delivery in 30 minutes. First order free delivery.&quot;</td>
<td>₹1,000–₹2,000</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Instagram launch campaign</strong></td>
<td>Sponsored posts targeting Guwahati, 18–35 age group. Creative: &quot;Need a formal shirt in 30 minutes? ThreadIt.&quot;</td>
<td>₹10,000–₹20,000</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>College campus activation</strong></td>
<td>Ambassadors distribute flyers + demo the app at canteens, hostels, common areas.</td>
<td>₹3,000–₹5,000 (flyers, snacks)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Vendor-driven sharing</strong></td>
<td>Deepa-type vendors share their ThreadIt store link on Instagram: &quot;Now you can order from my store online! 30-min delivery.&quot;</td>
<td>₹0 (organic — vendors share willingly because it drives their sales)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Launch day PR</strong></td>
<td>Pitch local media (Guwahati newspapers, local news websites, NE Now, EastMojo) with the story: &quot;Guwahati startup brings 30-minute clothing delivery.&quot;</td>
<td>₹0 (earned media)</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Total launch week budget: ₹20,000–₹50,000</strong></p>
<h3>Phase 2: Growth (Month 1–3)</h3>
<p><strong>Objective:</strong> Build sustainable growth channels. Move from push marketing to pull.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Channel</th>
<th>Strategy</th>
<th>CAC</th>
<th>Priority</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>Vendor-driven organic</strong></td>
<td>Every Deepa-type vendor shares their store link on Instagram/Facebook/WhatsApp. This is FREE customer acquisition driven by vendor self-interest.</td>
<td>₹10–₹30</td>
<td>🔴 Highest</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Referral program</strong></td>
<td>&quot;Invite a friend → you both get ₹50 off your next order.&quot; Simple, WhatsApp-shareable referral link.</td>
<td>₹50–₹80</td>
<td>🔴 High</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Instagram ads (targeted)</strong></td>
<td>Carousel ads showing &quot;before and after&quot; — 3-hour market trip vs. 30-min ThreadIt delivery. Target: Guwahati, 18–35, fashion/shopping interests.</td>
<td>₹80–₹150</td>
<td>🟡 Medium</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>WhatsApp marketing</strong></td>
<td>Send weekly &quot;New Arrivals&quot; messages to opt-in customers. Include product photos from newly onboarded stores.</td>
<td>₹5–₹10</td>
<td>🟡 Medium</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Google search ads</strong></td>
<td>Target &quot;buy clothes online Guwahati,&quot; &quot;clothing stores near me.&quot; Low volume but high intent.</td>
<td>₹100–₹200</td>
<td>🟢 Low (initially)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Repeat / retention</strong></td>
<td>Push notifications for repeat customers: &quot;New items at your favorite store!&quot; &quot;Your size just arrived at [store].&quot;</td>
<td>₹0</td>
<td>🔴 Highest</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
<blockquote>
<p>[!IMPORTANT]<br><strong>The cheapest growth channel is vendor-driven acquisition.</strong> When Deepa shares her ThreadIt store link on Instagram Stories, her 5,000 followers see it. Some download the app. Some order. This costs ThreadIt ₹0. <strong>This is why Deepa-type vendors are P0 for onboarding — they are both supply AND demand channels.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
